@@ -185,6 +185,52 @@ on this bootloader.
 Integration of this bootloader in the Zephyr build environment is available
 in the external `STM32 OEMxROT module`_.
 
+Board variants
+**************
+
+Three variants are available:
+
+- The default ``nucleo_n657x0_q`` target is a chainloaded application. It executes
+  directly from external flash (XIP) and uses AXISRAM1 for data and stacks.
+  Build it with ``--sysbuild`` to include MCUboot.
+- ``nucleo_n657x0_q//fsbl`` is a first-stage image loaded by the Boot ROM into
+  AXISRAM2 and programmed into external flash using ST-Link. Sysbuild uses this
+  variant for MCUboot, which initializes memory-mapped flash before starting
+  the XIP application.
+- ``nucleo_n657x0_q//sb`` runs in AXISRAM2 and is loaded through the USB serial
+  boot interface. It is not retained after power-off.
+
+The external MX25UM51245G flash has the following partitions:
+
+.. list-table::
+   :header-rows: 1
+
+   * - Partition
+     - Flash offset
+     - Size
+   * - MCUboot
+     - ``0x0``
+     - 256 KiB
+   * - Primary application
+     - ``0x40000``
+     - 4 MiB
+   * - Secondary application
+     - ``0x440000``
+     - 4 MiB
+   * - Storage
+     - ``0x840000``
+     - 8 MiB
+
+Flash is memory-mapped at ``0x70000000``. The partitions are contiguous and
+occupy the first 16 MiB plus 256 KiB of the 64 MiB flash. Storage ends at
+offset ``0x1040000`` and does not reach the final 32 bytes of the flash affected
+by the STM32N6 DQS wrap erratum (ES0620 Rev 1, section 2.4.5).
+Switching from the previous RAM-loaded image requires programming
+both MCUboot and the application; old images at flash offset zero are replaced.
+Changing partition offsets or sizes requires rebuilding and programming both
+images so that MCUboot and the application use the same partition layout.
+Existing storage data at the previous offset is not migrated automatically.
+
 Programming and Debugging
 *************************
 
